From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mercurious <dutch.money@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 19:52:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Mark the fork in driverInfo so a build is attributable at
 runtime

Stock and fork both report bare "Mesa <version>" from vulkaninfo, so with
several drivers selectable through the Pitstop DRIVER tab there was no way
to confirm which .so produced a given A/B result other than comparing
sha256 of the bound file. That is a real hazard for a project whose output
is A/B verdicts.

driverInfo becomes "Mesa <version> (git-<sha>) ETK-GTK". MESA_GIT_SHA1
supplies the per-build discriminator, and the literal suffix answers "is
this the fork at all?" at a glance. The numeric version is deliberately
left untouched: RPCS3 applies driver-version-keyed workarounds and parses
this string, so a non-numeric version suffix could change emulator
behaviour and confound the very comparison this is meant to enable.

This was previously a local uncommitted edit in the build tree, so it was
absent from the published series and would have been lost on the first
rebase. Carrying it as a patch fixes that.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index be6f618..8a53b4d 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -935,8 +935,18 @@ tu_get_physical_device_properties_1_2(struct tu_physical_device *pdevice,
    snprintf(p->driverName, VK_MAX_DRIVER_NAME_SIZE,
             "turnip Mesa driver");
    memset(p->driverInfo, 0, sizeof(p->driverInfo));
+   /* ETK: mark the fork in driverInfo so a build is attributable at runtime.
+    * PACKAGE_VERSION alone is identical between stock and fork, and Pitstop can
+    * hold several drivers at once, so an A/B result would otherwise be
+    * unattributable. MESA_GIT_SHA1 supplies the per-build discriminator (it is
+    * populated whenever git is on PATH at build time and the tree is a git
+    * checkout -- which prepare-fork-branch.sh always produces); the literal
+    * suffix makes "is this the fork at all?" answerable at a glance.
+    * Kept in the standard "Mesa <ver> (git-<sha>)" shape on purpose: RPCS3
+    * applies driver-version-keyed workarounds and parses this string, so the
+    * numeric version must stay untouched. */
    snprintf(p->driverInfo, VK_MAX_DRIVER_INFO_SIZE,
-            "Mesa " PACKAGE_VERSION MESA_GIT_SHA1);
+            "Mesa " PACKAGE_VERSION MESA_GIT_SHA1 " ETK-GTK");
    if (pdevice->info->chip >= 7) {
       p->conformanceVersion = (VkConformanceVersion) {
          .major = 1,
